xt\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Amplifications: <em>CDK4</em>, <em>CCND1</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Mutations: <em>SPRED1</em>, <em>PIK3CA</em>, <em>PTEN</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 157.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"210\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 157.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"210\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Monosomy: Chromosome&nbsp;3</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">a</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Co-mutations</span> may occur <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{28296713; 31320640}</span>. Targetable molecular alterations with therapeutic agents under investigation are those in <em>BRAF</em>, <em>KIT</em>, and <em>SF3B1</em> (inhibitor of alternative splicing). Evaluation of genomic alterations is critical to determine the efficacy of targeted therapies.</p>",
